## R75-audit rework (F-3/F-4/F-5/F-6) — 2026-09-22

Audit probe found three escape paths, all closed and now covered by a permanent
in-test corpus (runs every `turbo test`, not a one-off):
- template-literal specifier: import(`…`) — quote class gained the backtick
- subpath specifier: from "…/sub" / import("…/node") — tail accepts "/" now
- "//" inside a same-line string masking a trailing import — documented as an
  accepted blind spot (regex-literal ambiguity needs a real tokenizer)
F-4 cleanup: dead statSync import removed, SPEC escaping hoisted, redundant
export-* pattern dropped (the `from` leg covers it).
F-5 documented: `import type` goes red deliberately (strictness > "code path"
wording; the exempted `typeof import(…)` query is the sanctioned type channel).
F-6 documented: .pnpm first-match nondeterminism / ≤6 walk-up bound / single
SKIP line for three absent-causes — all recorded in test comments.

